 # Question schema
+
+PostgreSQL is the sole writable content authority. This page defines the schema-v4 quiz representation used in paired drafts/releases and deterministic JSON exports. Preserve array/choice order, exact authored strings, omitted optional fields, provided/verified answers and established IDs. Creates use server reservations within admitted allocation ceilings; legacy change-set descriptions below apply to reviewed import/fixture representations and never authorize a second writable bank. See [the recovery runbook](L4-authoritative-recovery.md).
 
 `src/content/questionBank.generated.json` has `schemaVersion: 4` and top-level `subjects`, `quizzes`, and `questions` collections. IDs are compact, type-prefixed strings: subjects use `s*`, quizzes use `q*`, and questions use `i*`. `Quiz.subjectId` is the only stored subject relationship; a question stores `quizId` but not a redundant subject ID. Questions are grouped by quiz in canonical array order; their position within each quiz determines the one-based learner display number. The [selected L3 database design](decisions/0005-paired-content-releases-and-postgres-schema.md) stores a separate zero-based global collection ordinal to reconstruct each complete array exactly. Migration `0001_content` implements this mapping and its constraints; the learner Postgres adapter now reconstructs response records from pinned normalized rows without changing optional presence or source/verified answers.
 
